  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The ambient sensing line has a vertical drop and rise of approximately one foot (creating a \"P-Trap\"). This tubing arrangement is located within five feet of the end of the sensing line, where the rain/wind cap is located. Any rainwater that may enter through the rain/wind cap would drain to and be captured by this P-trap, resulting in an incorrect ambient pressure in the ambient sensing line and erratic transmitter indication.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "historical design deficiency in sensing line routing allowing water intrusion",
    "provisional": true
  },
